# L3 — generalizza? Un solo meccanismo (kb/core/contact.p0), tre relazioni vere,
# un contatto ciascuna, domande su soggetti TENUTI FUORI dal contatto, e le
# trappole che misurano le false generalizzazioni e il ritiro per contatto.
# Si lancia a mano; i tempi non sono un cancello qui (vedi banco.p0t).
#
# SETUP DICHIARATO (§15.1): la KB viva collega gia' questi nomi alle loro
# relazioni. Si ritirano IN MEMORIA solo quei ponti, uno per nome:
#   birthplace -> born_in   (costruzione + frame)
#   material   -> made_of   (relation(material) e il suo relation_noun)
#   neighbour  -> borders   (il cue della catena compilata gen-chain10070)
# «food» -> eats NON e' nel banco: lo risponde un ramo compilato
# (animal_eats_answer) che nessun fatto ritira.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test setup]
!timeout 0
!forget construction_frame("@O is the birthplace of @S", "@S was born in @O", born_in)
!forget extract_frame("@O is the birthplace of @S", born_in)
!forget relation(material)
!forget relation_noun(made_of, material)
!forget intent_cue(10_memory_knowledge_chain10070, "neighbour")

[test base: i tre nomi non rispondono]
!timeout 0
> What is the birthplace of Galileo Galilei?
<! pisa
> What is the material of glass?
<! sand
> What is the neighbour of Germany?
<! Austria

# ── RELAZIONE 1: born_in ────────────────────────────────────────────────
[test r1 contatto]
!timeout 0
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so his birthplace is Ulm.
!query contact_bridge(birthplace, born_in)
[test r1 trasferimento]
!timeout 0
> What is the birthplace of Galileo Galilei?
<~ pisa
> What is the birthplace of Christopher Columbus?
<~ genoa

# ── RELAZIONE 2: made_of ────────────────────────────────────────────────
[test r2 contatto]
!timeout 0
> Steel is made of iron, so iron is its material.
!query contact_bridge(material, made_of)
[test r2 trasferimento]
!timeout 0
> What is the material of glass?
<~ sand
> What is the material of paper?
<~ wood pulp

# ── RELAZIONE 3: borders ────────────────────────────────────────────────
[test r3 contatto]
!timeout 0
> France borders Spain, so Spain is its neighbour.
!query contact_bridge(neighbour, borders)
[test r3 trasferimento]
!timeout 0
> What is the neighbour of Germany?
<~ austria

# ── TRAPPOLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[test t1 inciso: un ruolo solo, nessun episodio]
!timeout 0
> Galileo Galilei, an astronomer, was born in Pisa.
!query! contact_episode(astronomer, $R, $E)

[test t2 coincidenza: nasce un'ipotesi SBAGLIATA]
!timeout 0
> Rome is in Italy, and Rome is its capital.
!query contact_bridge(capital, located_in)

[test t3 ritiro per contatto: una correzione ordinaria la fa cadere]
!timeout 0
> Milan is in Italy, but Milan isn't its capital.
!query contact_counter(capital, located_in, ep(milan, italy, o))
!query! contact_bridge(capital, located_in)

[test t4 le ipotesi giuste non cadono con quella sbagliata]
!timeout 0
!query contact_bridge(birthplace, born_in)
!query contact_bridge(material, made_of)
!query contact_bridge(neighbour, borders)

[test t5 la premessa e' del turno che ha usato l'ipotesi, non dei seguenti]
!timeout 0
> What is the material of glass?
<! birthplace
